---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Teaching"
  description="Plant Physiology with a course-based research experience, Introduction to Plant Sciences, and Root to Shoot, a set of interactive modules for Plant Physiology."
>
  <h1 class="text-2xl">Teaching</h1>

  <section>
    <h2 class="section-title">Plant Physiology (BIO 332)</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-measure">
      An upper-division lecture course, 100 students in Fall 2026. Every student takes part in a
      course-based research experience built on my research: they work with real synchrotron microCT
      scans of plants under drought and recovery, and their work feeds a dataset built with the
      Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory. Two undergraduates from my lab help lead it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="section-title">Introduction to Plant Sciences (BIO 106)</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-measure">An introductory course with laboratory.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-measure text-muted">
      I also teach Advanced Irrigation and Nutrient Management (AGPS 415), Research Methods for Crop
      and Soil Sciences (AGPS 350), Plants, Agriculture, and Climate Change (AGPS 209), and Principles
      of Viticulture (AGPS 213).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="section-title">Root to Shoot</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-measure">
      Root to Shoot is a set of interactive modules for Plant Physiology; the first module, The Water Path,
      covers the water relations units.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-measure">
      <a href="/water-path/">The Water Path</a>: students predict before each figure, work with data from
      my lab, and every number carries a badge saying whether it is measured, derived or illustrative.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
